### Review Summary

The runtime currently tracks metrics internally (`MetricsTracker`) but does not expose them to the client. The client HUD needs to display these metrics (e.g., `turnsTotal`, `invalidOutputCount`, `queuedActions`) to provide feedback on simulation health and agent behavior.

**Root Cause:**
1.  **Protocol Gap:** The `ServerMessage` type in `@codexgame/protocol` lacks a definition for a `runtime.metrics` message type.
2.  **State Propagation:** The `GameRuntimeServer` does not emit the metrics snapshot to connected clients.
3.  **Client Gap:** The client `App.tsx` does not have state to receive or display these metrics.

**Proposed Fix:**
1.  **Protocol (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`):** Add `RuntimeMetrics` type and a new `runtime.metrics` server message variant.
2.  **Runtime (`apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`):** Emit the metrics snapshot periodically (e.g., in `sendWorldSnapshot` or a dedicated `emitMetrics` call) to ensure the HUD stays updated without excessive overhead.
3.  **Client (`apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`):** Add state to receive `runtime.metrics` messages and display them in the HUD.
4.  **Tests (`apps/game-runtime/test/ui-contract.integration.test.ts`):** Add a contract test to verify the new message type encodes/decodes correctly.

### Changes

#### 1. `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`
Add the `RuntimeMetrics` type and the new `runtime.metrics` message variant.

```typescript
// ... existing imports

export type RuntimeMetrics = {
  turnsTotal: number;
  invalidOutputCount: number;
  actionAppliedCount: number;
  actionRejectedCount: number;
  queuedActions: number;
};

// ... existing types ...

export type ServerMessage =
  // ... existing variants ...
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "runtime.metrics";
      payload: RuntimeMetrics;
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "error";
      payload: {
        code: string;
        message: string;
        recoverable: boolean;
      };
    };

// ... existing schemas ...

const clientMessageSchema = z.discriminatedUnion("type", [
  // ... existing client schemas ...
]);

// Note: Server messages are not validated by clientMessageSchema, but the type definition is required for the client to parse them.
```

#### 2. `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`
Emit metrics periodically. We will add a dedicated `emitMetrics` call and invoke it in `sendWorldSnapshot` (which is already called frequently) to ensure the HUD updates without adding a separate timer.

```typescript
// ... existing imports ...

export class GameRuntimeServer {
  // ... existing fields ...

  private emitMetrics(): void {
    const metrics = this.metrics.snapshot();
    this.emitMessage({
      version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
      type: "runtime.metrics",
      payload: metrics
    });
  }

  // ... existing methods ...

  private sendWorldSnapshot(): void {
    if (!this.simulation) {
      return;
    }
    const snapshot = this.simulation.getSnapshot();
    const content = this.contentStore.getContent();
    this.emitMessage({
      version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
      type: "world.snapshot",
      payload: {
        // ... existing payload ...
      }
    });
    // Emit metrics alongside world snapshot to keep HUD in sync
    this.emitMetrics();
  }

  // ... rest of class ...
}
```

#### 3. `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`
Add state to hold metrics and display them in the HUD.

```typescript
// ... existing imports ...

export default function App() {
  // ... existing state ...

  const [runtimeMetrics, setRuntimeMetrics] = useState<RuntimeMetrics | null>(null);

  // ... existing effects ...

  ws.onmessage = (event) => {
    const message = JSON.parse(event.data as string) as ServerMessage;

    switch (message.type) {
      // ... existing cases ...
      case "runtime.metrics":
        setRuntimeMetrics(message.payload);
        return;
      // ... existing cases ...
    }
  };

  // ... existing logic ...

  return (
    // ... existing JSX ...
    <div className="game-topbar">
      <span className="pill">Runtime: {connected ? "connected" : "offline"}</span>
      <span className="pill">Phase: {phase}</span>
      <span className="pill">Latency: {latencyMs}ms</span>
      <span className="pill">Model: {runtimeModel ?? "default"}</span>
      <span className="pill">
        Effort: {runtimeEffort} | Scheduler: {runtimeSchedulerMs || "-"}ms
      </span>
      {/* New Metrics Pill */}
      {runtimeMetrics && (
        <span className="pill">
          Turns: {runtimeMetrics.turnsTotal} | Rejected: {runtimeMetrics.actionRejectedCount} | Queue: {runtimeMetrics.queuedActions}
        </span>
      )}
    </div>
    // ... rest of JSX ...
  );
}
```

